{
  "contract": "fleet",
  "about": "Which Claude Code accounts may work in which projects (spec flow-multiproject 8.1-8.2 in dork-labs/dorkos; contract 4.2.0). The rules live in DorkOS's config.json under runtimes.claudeCode: each registered row's 'onlyProjects' (a list of project roots, or null/absent for any project), Main's rule 'defaultAccountOnlyProjects' (the same, for the id 'default', which has no row), and 'projectAccounts' (project root to { allow: [account ids] }; a project with no entry allows every account; 'default' may be listed). An account may work in a project only when BOTH rules allow it. An account rule that is a list never allows 'no project': a folder in no git repository. 'No project' has no project rule. A project is the git main checkout a folder belongs to: input.git maps a folder to the main checkout git reports for it (a linked worktree and a subfolder map to their main checkout); a folder absent from input.git, or input.folder null, is in no project. Roots are compared canonically: without a trailing slash, and through input.realpath (a folder to its real path; a folder absent from it is already real), on both the stored roots and the project's. A stored value of the wrong shape reads as no rule (a reader never fails a launch over a hand edit). Call eligibility(config, account, projectRoot) with projectRoot the canonical root (or null). expected.eligible says whether the account may work there; when it may not, expected.reason is 'only-projects' (the account's own rule) or 'project-allowlist' (the project's rule), and the account rule is checked first. flow's mayServe for Claude Code routing must agree with this for every case; DorkOS enforces it at every place an account is picked.",
  "cases": [
    {
      "name": "no rules: any account works in any project",
      "input": {
        "config": {
          "runtimes": {
            "claudeCode": {
              "accounts": [
                {
                  "id": "work",
                  "path": "/home/me/.claude-work",
                  "label": "Work",
                  "color": null
                },
                {
                  "id": "personal",
                  "path": "/home/me/.claude2",
                  "label": null,
                  "color": null
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        },
        "account": "work",
        "folder": "/work/client-app",
        "git": {
          "/work/client-app": "/work/client-app"
        }
      },
      "expected": {
        "eligible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "no rules: any account works in a folder in no project",
